        "orario": "15:24",
        "timestamp": 1774963448,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. EU ministers in Kyiv to look at justice for crimes committed in Bucha Europe Issued on: 31/03/2026 - 15:24 Modified: 31/03/2026 - 15:37 EU diplomats are travelling to Ukraine to mark the fourth anniversary of the massacre in the city of Bucha. It occurred only weeks into the war: after Russia evacuate the town, returnees found hundreds of bodies of men, women, children and elderly people who had been mass executed. FRANCE 24's Douglas Herbert looks back on an event that became a symbol of what many towns in Ukraine have experienced since the start of the war. EU ministers commemorate Bucha massacre and reaffirm support to Ukraine 31/03/2026 Europe Ukraine's Bucha commemorates four years since massacre 31/03/2026 Europe Police arrest two more over attempted attack on US bank HQ in Paris 30/03/2026 Europe Paintings by Renoir, Cézanne and Matisse stolen from Italian museum 30/03/2026 Europe Ukraine signs defence agreements with Gulf Nations eager to fend off Iranian drones 30/03/2026 Middle East Russian strikes on Ukraine kill at least 5 28/03/2026 Europe Deadly Russian strikes damage port, maternity hospital 28/03/2026 Europe North Korea's Kim Jong Un gifted gun by Belarusian leader 27/03/2026 Europe 'Return hubs' for migrants clear EU parliament hurdle 26/03/2026 Europe"
